# Social Guest Inbox — agent reference

Guest Inbox at **property** and **parking** scopes (org-level Inbox UI removed). Phase 1 ships **Meta** (Facebook Messenger + Instagram DMs) and **Web** (on-site guest chat from property pages). Facebook / Instagram post comments are **out of scope** for this inbox and should not be surfaced in UI, webhook handling, or docs. TikTok / Airbnb messaging APIs are **out of scope** (partnership / approval barriers) — do not show Coming soon placeholders or fake connectivity.

## Routes

| Scope    | Path                                         |
| -------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Property | `/org/:orgSlug/property/:propertySlug/inbox` |
| Parking  | `/org/:orgSlug/parking/:parkingSlug/inbox`   |

`/org/:orgSlug/inbox` redirects to Properties.

## Permissions

| Property / parking | Capability                                            |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `inbox:view`       | Read threads and messages                             |
| `inbox:reply`      | Send replies                                          |
| `inbox:manage`     | Channels + (property only) quick replies / automation |

Keep in sync: `propertyTeamPermissions.ts`, `parkingTeamPermissions.ts` and UI team constants. Org `org:inbox:*` permissions were removed.

## Data scope

- Every row keyed by `organization_id`. Use `resolveInboxAccess(req, capability)` — requires `property_id` or `parking_id` + `inbox:*`.
- Org Meta default: `social_channel_connections` with `property_id`/`parking_id` null. Overrides set one of those FKs.
- **First Meta connect from a property** (no org-default yet) writes the **org-default** row so Marketing and other units can inherit.
- Effective Meta = override if connected, else org default (`metaInboxScope.ts`). Inherited Meta threads = full Page inbox (1A).
- Webhook handler is public but **must** verify `X-Hub-Signature-256` and dedupe via `social_webhook_events`. Resolve by `meta_page_id` to the owning connection row.
- Tokens encrypted with `META_INBOX_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY`.
- Org reconnect/disconnect must **not** delete property/parking override rows (`metaInboxLifecycle.ts`).
- Marketing publish uses **org-default** Meta (first property connect establishes it).

## Meta messaging rules

- **24-hour window:** outbound DMs only when `messaging_window_expires_at` > now (set from last inbound). **Does not apply to `platform=web`.**
- **Webhook-first:** Conversations API backfill on connect only; do not poll in a loop.
- **App Review:** production requires Advanced Access — see `docs/archive/operations/meta-app-review.md`.

## AI auto-reply

- No auto-fill-on-open — operators trigger AI drafts manually via the composer's **Suggest** (sparkles) button on any thread. There is no `auto_reply_mode = draft` UI path; the column stays in `social_inbox_settings` for backward compat but is not surfaced.
- Auto-send (`send`, `auto_reply_mode = 'send'`) requires explicit org opt-in in Automation tab (property Manage → Automation).
- Never auto-reply outside Meta messaging window (**Meta only** — web chat has no 24h window).
- Platform toggles under auto-send: Facebook, Instagram, **Chat** (`platform_toggles.web`).
- Web auto-send runs from `guest-web-chat-messages` POST via `webInboxAutoReply.ts` after guest inbound.
- Text auto-reply uses the same closed guest tool layer as voice (`guestReceptionistTools.ts` + `guestReceptionistTurn.ts`): Flash-Lite, ≤2 tool rounds. Web may include one maps URL or markdown table; Meta is flattened to prose. Parking threads use `get_parking_facts`.
- Cooldown is per inbound message (a new guest question after an AI reply reopens). At 10 AI replies per conversation per hour, insert the host-will-reply line once per hour (`AUTO_REPLY_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED_LINE`).
- Flag outbound AI messages with `is_ai_generated = true`.
- **Manage AI response** (Automation → Manage button → `InboxAiResponseDialog`) edits `ai_system_prompt` — free-text org **Tone & rules** layered on top of the base prompt in `socialInboxAiService.ts`. This custom text is additive; it never replaces Known facts, quick-reply guidance, or the mandatory safety policy. Field help lives on a **?** tooltip (`FieldLabel`). Includes a **Reset to default** action that fills `DEFAULT_AI_RESPONSE_CONTEXT`.

## AI grounding & guard

Before every AI call, `suggestInboxReply` builds a guest-safe facts bundle via **`inboxAiGuestContext.ts`** and runs output through **`inboxAiSafetyGuard.ts`**.

**Allowed in facts (org/property scoped):**

- Active property list (org-level fallback when thread has no `property_id`)
- Property name, full address, city, residence, tower/unit, floor, capacity, check-in/out times, map link
- Payment methods with account name and number (same as guest form / property settings)
- Weekday/weekend rates, security deposit, pet fee, parking rate, holiday % rules
- Amenities, house rules, cancellation policy (title + description)
- **Development/residence facts** (when property `residence_name` matches a development): development name, amenities, pool fee, pool schedule, guest requirements, guide entries, document requirement labels, other important info — via `_shared/developmentGuestInfo.ts`
- Today/tomorrow availability, next open check-in dates, blocked stay date ranges
- Inquiry-date availability + estimated stay total when thread has inquiry dates
- Booking form URL, calendar URL
- Org quick reply snippets (`social_reply_templates`, platform-filtered) as fallback when property facts are incomplete

**Never in facts or replies:**

- Other guests' PII (names, email, phone, IDs, receipts)
- Finance (revenue, expenses, profit, ledger rows)
- Maintenance/reminders, Telegram settings, OAuth tokens, internal ops fields
- Ungrounded PHP amounts (guard rejects amounts not derivable from allowed pricing facts)

**Enforcement:**

- Facts injected into user prompt under `Known facts (property/booking data + quick reply snippets):`
- `classifyGuestInquiryIntent` distinguishes normal vs sensitive guest asks
- `assertSafeGuestReply` blocks other-guest name leaks, owner/internal topics, ungrounded prices; allows polite refusals on sensitive asks
- On flag: return safe fallback copy; `social-inbox-ai-suggest` sets `flagged: true` for operator UI

**Do not** wire guest AI to admin endpoints (`list-bookings`, `app-settings`, `finance-*`, `maintenance-*`) or raw `guest_submissions` rows with PII.

## Edge functions

| Function                                             | Auth            |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |
| `meta-inbox-oauth-start`                             | JWT + org       |
| `meta-inbox-oauth-callback`                          | Public redirect |
| `meta-inbox-status` / `disconnect`                   | JWT + org       |
| `meta-inbox-webhook`                                 | Public (signed) |
| `social-inbox-threads` / `messages` / `send`         | JWT + org       |
| `guest-web-chat-start` / `guest-web-chat-messages`   | JWT (guest)     |
| `social-inbox-templates` / `settings` / `ai-suggest` | JWT + org       |

All JWT routes: `verify_jwt = false` in config + `serveAuthenticated` + in-handler checks.

## UI

- Feature folder: `ui/src/features/dashboard/inbox/`
- Mobile: master–detail with back button on conversation view
- Realtime: Supabase channel on `social_messages` + `social_conversations` for org id

## Don'ts

- Don't leak cross-org data in webhooks (resolve connection by `meta_page_id`).
- Don't scrape Airbnb/TikTok or claim inbox connectivity without official messaging APIs.
- Don't skip route guide + `docs/PROJECT.md` updates when changing behavior.
